<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Blue Angels Enlisted Recruitment Information</title>
</head>
<body>
  <header>
    <h1>Blue Angels Enlisted Recruitment Information</h1>
    <p>An unofficial class project for IT371: Web Design and Development.</p>
  </header>

  <nav>
    <a href="#concept">Website Concept</a> |
    <a href="#audience">Target Audience</a> |
    <a href="#roles">Enlisted Roles</a> |
    <a href="#resources">Resources</a>
  </nav>

  <main>
    <section id="concept">
      <h2>Website Concept</h2>
      <p>
        This website is designed to educate Sailors and Marines about enlisted
        opportunities with the Blue Angels. The goal is to explain what different
        enlisted jobs contribute, how those jobs support the demonstration mission,
        and how interested service members can begin learning about the process.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="audience">
      <h2>Target Audience</h2>
      <p>
        The target audience includes active-duty Sailors and Marines who are
        interested in learning more about enlisted opportunities on the team.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="roles">
      <h2>Enlisted Roles</h2>
      <p>
        Enlisted members support the mission through maintenance, administration,
        logistics, supply, public affairs, and other important support functions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="resources">
      <h2>Resources</h2>
      <p>
        This site is an unofficial educational project and does not replace official
        Navy, Marine Corps, or Blue Angels guidance.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer>
    <p>&copy; 2026 Greg Dungey - IT371 Class Project</p>
  </footer>
